# --- App ---
# Used for email confirmation and OAuth return URLs when `window` is unavailable.
# Production example: https://iepmobile.threadsail.io
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Supabase (required) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_DEFAULT_KEY=your_anon_publishable_key

# Server-only (if you use service role anywhere)
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional: allow “Add 10 test students” on /dashboard/students when not in NODE_ENV=development.
# ALLOW_SEED_TEST_STUDENTS=true

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google sign-in (Supabase Auth — provider "google")
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web).
# Google Auth Platform → Data Access (Scopes): enable openid, userinfo.email,
#   userinfo.profile (recommended; configure in Google Cloud, not in app code).
#
# If Google shows “This app’s request is invalid” / Error 400: use a Web OAuth client,
# fix redirect URI to …supabase.co/auth/v1/callback, complete the OAuth consent screen,
# use user type “External” for public sign-in, and sign in from a normal browser (not
# an embedded WebView). Do not paste Android/iOS client IDs into Supabase → Google.
# Authorized redirect URI (Supabase receives the callback):
#   https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# Authorized JavaScript origins: your app origin(s), e.g. http://localhost:3000 and prod.
#
# Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Google: enable; paste Web client ID +
# client secret (not in this file). Same /auth/callback redirect URLs as below.
#
# What users see on Google’s screen:
# - App title / logo: Google Cloud → Auth Platform → Branding (or OAuth consent
#   screen) — set App name (e.g. IEPmobile), logo, home page. Not controlled in code.
# - “Continue to …supabase.co”: that’s the OAuth redirect host (your Supabase URL).
#   To use your own domain there, add a Supabase Custom Domain (paid) or vanity
#   subdomain, then add the new …/auth/v1/callback in Google and use that URL in
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL. See: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/platform/custom-domains
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Microsoft sign-in via Supabase (Entra ID / “Azure” provider)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A UUID-style “Client ID” in Supabase is almost always Microsoft Entra ID
# (Azure AD), not Google. Credentials stay in Supabase only — not in this file.
#
# 1) Microsoft Entra admin center (https://entra.microsoft.com/) → Applications
#    → App registrations → your app → copy Application (client) ID + create a
#    client secret. Authentication → add a platform → Web.
#    Redirect URI (Supabase receives the OAuth callback):
#      https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#
# 2) Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Sign In / Providers → Azure
#      https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/YOUR_PROJECT_REF/auth/providers
#    Enable Azure, paste Entra Application (client) ID and client secret.
#    The app calls signInWithOAuth({ provider: "azure" | "google" }) — AuthForm.
#
# 3) Supabase → Authentication → URL configuration
#    - Site URL: app origin only (e.g. http://localhost:3000 or
#      https://iepmobile.threadsail.io) — not /dashboard
#    - Additional Redirect URLs (OAuth must return here first; exact path, no ?query):
#        http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#        https://iepmobile.threadsail.io/auth/callback
#      If you use ?next= on the callback URL, add a wildcard e.g. …/auth/callback**
#      or OAuth can fall back to Site URL with bad_oauth_state. This app stores
#      post-login path in a short-lived cookie instead.
#
# `/auth/callback` exchanges the `code` for a session (`auth/callback/route.ts`).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
